---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const chapters = (await getCollection('guide')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.step - b.data.step,
);
---
<Base
  title="Working with Coding Agents — a field guide"
  description="Concrete patterns for working with coding agents, one step at a time — each with an optional paste-into-Claude setup. Distilled from measured usage."
>
  <p class="kicker">
    Lemon Agent № 3 · {chapters.length} steps
    <span class="badge draft">draft</span>
  </p>
  <h1>Working with Coding Agents<br />— a field guide</h1>

  <p>
    Concrete patterns that survive real use: what to watch out for, and
    the habits worth building — verification loops, design interviews,
    adversarial reviews, orchestration, tools, generated UIs. Written for
    humans to adopt <strong>one step at a time</strong>; every step ends
    with an optional <em>paste-into-Claude</em> block that sets it up for
    you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Little here is new, and that's the point: most steps are old
    software maxims — TDD, design review, the Unix philosophy,
    pre-commit hooks — refitted for agents. Each chapter names its
    ancestor under <em>"you've met this before."</em>
  </p>

  <blockquote class="prov">
    Distilled from one practitioner's measured usage — dozens of logged
    sessions, the incidents that recurred, and the patterns that stopped
    them. <strong>v0</strong> — step slugs are stable; chapters may be
    cut or reordered before 1.0.
  </blockquote>

  <h2>The steps</h2>
  <p class="section-note">
    Ordered by leverage-per-effort, but every step stands alone — start
    where it hurts. In a hurry, step 0 is the whole baseline in one
    paste.
  </p>
  <ol class="toc">
    {chapters.map((ch) => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/guide/${ch.id}/`}>
          <span class="toc-step">{String(ch.data.step).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <span class="toc-title">{ch.data.title.replace(/^Step \d+ — /, '')}</span>
        </a>
        <p class="toc-blurb">{ch.data.description}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2>Check your work against</h2>
  <p>
    The guide's watch-out half lives in two numbered failure lists —
    every "watch out" above cites them by id:
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/prose-failure-list/">The Prose Failure List</a> (PF-01…24,
    taste) · <a href="/agent-workflow-failure-list/">The Agent Workflow
    Failure List</a> (AF-01…18, verification).
  </p>

  <p class="backlink">
    <a href="/">← Lemon Agent</a> · for agents: raw chapters at
    <code>/guide/*.md</code>, catalog at
    <a href="/catalog.json">/catalog.json</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .prov {
    margin: 1.4rem 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--chartreuse);
    background: var(--note-bg);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .section-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 0; }

  .toc { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.1rem 0 0.5rem; display: grid; gap: 0.85rem; }
  .toc a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.7em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .toc a:hover .toc-title { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .toc-step {
    color: var(--chip-ink);
    background: var(--chartreuse);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.05em 0.4em;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .toc-title { font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .toc-blurb { margin: 0.15rem 0 0 2.6em; font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
